id: pm-jev-ny9g
title: pm-jev provider config and privacy gate
description: Provider selection from pm settings (providers.ollama defaults; jev settings section; env overrides PM_JEV_BASE_URL/PM_JEV_MODEL). Hosted TypeSafe requires TYPESAFE_API_KEY plus explicit jev.allow_external=true opt-in; refuse otherwise (adversarially tested).
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[1]: "pkg:pm-jev"
created_at: "2026-10-05T04:38:45.443Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-12T05:57:33.639Z"
assignee: pi-jev
claim_principal: pi-jev
author: pi-glm
parent: pm-jev-0w3q
comments[7]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-05T05:17:11.002Z",codex-sol,"Adversarial tests now reject missing or string-valued hosted opt-in before any HTTP request, including provider=ollama with an external URL override. Redirects are refused, request/response logging is disabled, and transport errors omit reflected provider bodies. HTTP tests exercise 429/529 retry limits, total deadlines, timeouts, unreachable endpoints, missing models, and malformed answers before apply."
  "2026-10-05T05:56:45.157Z",codex-sol,"Verified the shared 17 command/transport tests within the 86-test all-source suite: real TypeSafe SDK HTTP, host extension harness, and isolated real pm projects. All source coverage dimensions are 100%; live local tev1 schema/plausibility and packed npm/Bun installation acceptance passed. Implementation and receipts are linked in README.md and docs/v0-validation.md. Leaving this item in progress for orchestrator verification and closure."
  "2026-10-11T05:14:19.234Z",codex-sol,"Exact remaining gap on main 7c0f0e0: index.ts:275 resolveJevEndpoint documents typed providers.ollama fallback, and this item description requires it, but implementation reads only jev settings, environment and built-in defaults (index.ts:279-293). The runtime/privacy acceptance otherwise passes: provider settings refuse every external command before any HTTP request; hosted credentials require HTTPS and custom origins require an environment override; malformed HTTP answers fail before apply and redirect targets receive no state. No provider fallback regression exists; leave in_progress with this gap. Hosted live acceptance is separately pending. Fresh main acceptance: node --test test/agent-ux.test.ts test/decisions.test.ts test/transport.test.ts test/release-workflow.test.ts test/calibration.test.ts passed 51/51, zero failures/skips. Tracker schema has no review status, so status stays in_progress; not closed. Cross-reference docs/tracker-reconciliation.md; line numbers refer to checked main."
  "2026-10-12T05:54:19.667Z",pi-jev,"Claimed the typed providers.ollama fallback gap: resolveJevEndpoint must read pm's typed providers.ollama base_url/model through the SDK's readSettings when the jev section does not set them. Keeping the documented precedence: environment overrides, then jev settings, then typed providers.ollama, then built-in defaults; the providers.ollama section only feeds the local ollama provider so hosted TypeSafe resolution is unchanged. No privacy-rule change: non-loopback URLs (from any source) still require explicit allow_external opt-in, hosted destinations require HTTPS plus PM_JEV_BASE_URL for custom origins, and settings reads never spawn external commands."
  "2026-10-12T05:56:48.915Z",pi-jev,"Design delivered on feat/providers-ollama-fallback: resolveJevEndpoint now consults a new readOllamaProviderSettings helper that reads the tracker's typed providers.ollama base_url/model through the SDK's readSettings projection (no raw settings.json parsing). The helper is called only when the selected provider is ollama, so hosted TypeSafe resolution is byte-for-byte unchanged and an Ollama endpoint can never become a hosted credential destination. readSettings is total by contract (absent/malformed settings resolve to typed defaults whose providers.ollama values are empty strings) and stringSetting treats blanks as unset, so the built-in defaults still apply when the section is not configured. Full precedence as documented in the docstring and README: environment overrides, then the jev section, then typed providers.ollama, then built-in defaults. Every privacy rule is preserved: a non-loopback URL sourced from providers.ollama still requires jev.allow_external=true opt-in, hosted credentials still require HTTPS with custom origins gated behind PM_JEV_BASE_URL, and settings resolution still never spawns external commands."
  "2026-10-12T05:57:32.994Z",pi-jev,"Behavioural revert proof: with only the changed resolution source (index.ts) reverted to the base revision, the linked regression suite fails 3 of 18 tests — exactly the three behavioural providers.ollama cases (endpoint supply, precedence, blanks/built-ins fall-through and the non-loopback opt-in gate) — while the fourth new test, the invariant guard 'hosted typesafe resolution never adopts the ollama provider endpoint', passes on both revisions by design because pre-change code ignored provider settings entirely. With the change restored the suite is 18/18 pass, 0 fail, 0 skipped. The all-source suite (node --test test/*.test.ts) passes 131/131 on the branch, and the same command ran through the linked pm test surface with status=passed, exit 0."
  "2026-10-12T05:57:33.639Z",pi-jev,"Manual live acceptance run (single run, outside the test suite, per the item's allowance for the local Ollama serving tev1:4b): a scratch tracker whose settings configure only the typed providers.ollama section (stock local Ollama endpoint, model tev1:4b), with no jev section and no environment overrides, resolved to that endpoint and ran one real jev triage decision against the local Ollama: model tev1:4b, type proposed Issue with ~0.98 confidence, priority level 0, no fields applied, real token usage recorded. The test suite itself contains no live model queries — all HTTP boundaries are deterministic loopback servers."
